From 1705dee6c3001977dab2ca5c0f973fb018c4e83c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: youkorr <96953496+youkorr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:33:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(esp_lvgl_adapter): draw rotated DOUBLE_DIRECT displays
 in the panel's orientation

Add CONFIG_ESP_LVGL_ADAPTER_ROTATE_IN_DRAW (LVGL v9, off by default). With
rotation 90/180/270 and DOUBLE_DIRECT on an RGB or MIPI DSI panel, LVGL draws
straight into the panel's two frame buffers in the panel's orientation,
through LVGL's matrix rotation (lv_display_set_matrix_rotation) and the
lv_draw_ortho draw unit, and the flush only switches buffers, as unrotated
DOUBLE_DIRECT does. Nothing is drawn upright and copied rotated afterwards,
and 2 frame buffers are needed instead of 3.

lv_draw_ortho draws widgets with LVGL's software renderer into a small tile
in internal RAM; on chips with a PPA the PPA rotates each tile into the frame
buffer while the CPU draws the next one, and fills plain rectangles. Every
PPA wait is bounded; a PPA that stops answering falls back to the CPU. Blocks
the v5.5 driver would hang on at 90/270 (DIG-734) are split before they are
sent.

The lvgl9 test app runs its tests on a rotated DOUBLE_DIRECT display when the
option is set; sdkconfig.ci.rotate_in_draw builds that for esp32p4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TUymkF8hVRdZRPiwDncnJt
